blocks.en:
To verify that our MLLM-based protocol produces scores consistent with human judgment, we randomly sample 20
videos and recruit 5 annotators to score each along the same five dimensions using a standardized rubric;
inter-annotator agreement reaches Krippendorff’s α = 0.70 \alpha=0.70 . Over all 100 scored items (20 videos × \times 5 dimensions), Table 3 reports Pearson r = 0.73 r=0.73 and Spearman ρ = 0.70 \rho=0.70 , demonstrating substantial alignment between automated and human evaluation.

